# openXwallet code owners.
#
# The floor is narrow on purpose: the checkers, the content they check, the
# pins that decide WHICH vendored artifact and WHICH openWallet they read, and
# the workflows that decide whether they run at all. A pull request that could
# change what runs cannot clear itself.

# The conformance validator ENTRYPOINT. It composes the pinned openWallet core
# with the adapter's rules (rule (t), the register reader, the hermes binding),
# and every consumer's required check runs it; a change here is a
# contract-behaviour change.
/scripts/validate-openxwallet.py   @brettheap

# The syntax-gate entrypoint, delegating to the pinned core's.
/scripts/wallet-yaml-syntax-gate.py   @brettheap

# The pin verifier: the only thing standing between a swapped vendored schema
# and a validator that checks presence rather than identity.
/scripts/verify-contract-pin.py   @brettheap

# The openWallet pin verifier: the only thing standing between a moved gitlink,
# a code leg out of lockstep or a drifted digest and a validator that runs
# whatever is checked out under openWallet/.
/scripts/verify-openwallet-pin.py   @brettheap

# The neutrality gate: the proof that the composed run is byte-identical to the
# pre-split validator, and that the one new line on this tree is the declared
# one. A pull request that weakened it could hide a changed finding.
/scripts/neutrality-gate.py   @brettheap

# The manifest, the changelog, the vendored artifact and the three adapter
# negatives.
/contracts/   @brettheap

# WHICH openWallet root commit, WHICH code-leg commit and WHICH eight digests
# the composed validator runs against. Already under /contracts/; named so its
# reason is on record, as /contract_pin.yaml's is.
/contracts/openwallet-pin.yaml   @brettheap

# WHICH openxFactory commit and WHICH digest the vendored artifact must match.
/contract_pin.yaml   @brettheap

# WHERE the openWallet submodule is cloned from and WHERE it mounts. The
# gitlink fixes the commit; this file names the repository and the path that
# the init lines and the verifier read.
/.gitmodules   @brettheap

# The openWallet gitlink: WHICH openWallet root this repository runs. It moves
# only together with /contracts/openwallet-pin.yaml, in one commit.
/openWallet   @brettheap

# Whether the checks run, in what order, and under which status-check token.
/.github/workflows/   @brettheap
